# C11

- C11 only. No C++ files, no `new`/`std::`, no exceptions.
- `-Wall -Wextra -Werror`. No VLAs. Check every `malloc`/`fopen`/`read`.
- One concern per file, keep units under ~500 lines.
- Errors: return a `tny_err` with a stable code and message; do not swallow.

```c
/* ❌ BAD */
char *p = malloc(n);
memcpy(p, src, n);

/* ✅ GOOD */
char *p = malloc(n);
if (!p)
    return tny_err_oom("session buffer");
memcpy(p, src, n);
```

Vendor only the libraries in `docs/language-and-runtime.md` (yyjson, wslay, nanopb, tiny HTTP). No libuv, ncurses, protobuf C++, or gRPC.
